+<
+			  The same check applies to `:try`: the `:try` body
+			  and all `:catch` blocks must terminate, unless a
+			  terminating `:finally` block overrides them.  In a
+			  loop, `:break` and `:continue` make later commands
+			  in the loop body unreachable, but do not make
+			  commands after the loop unreachable.  For example,
+			  when every branch of an `:if`/`:else` returns, a
+			  command after `:endif` is unreachable:
